{"summary":"Three defects found: POST /users stores age without validation, GET /orders hides store failures behind an empty 200 response, and elapsed() returns seconds although it is documented to return milliseconds.","sourceRefs":[{"relPath":"src/handlers/user.ts","startLine":34,"endLine":34},{"relPath":"src/handlers/orders.ts","startLine":51,"endLine":57},{"relPath":"src/lib/format.ts","startLine":3,"endLine":10}],"unresolvedQuestions":[],"outcome":"findings","findings":[{"id":"F1","title":"age is not validated on user creation","severity":"high","category":"validation","description":"createUser casts body.age to number without checking it. Negative, fractional, or non-numeric ages are stored and returned, although docs/api.md requires a whole number from 0 to 150 and the README requires 400 VALIDATION_FAILED on bad input. requireNonNegativeInteger in src/lib/validate.ts already implements the check.","sourceRefs":[{"relPath":"src/handlers/user.ts","startLine":34,"endLine":34},{"relPath":"src/lib/validate.ts","startLine":29,"endLine":41}]},{"id":"F2","title":"listOrders swallows store errors and returns an empty 200","severity":"high","category":"error_handling","description":"When the order store throws, listOrders answers 200 with an empty body. This breaks the public response format ({ data } | { error }) and hides the failure. It should call sendError so the client receives 500 INTERNAL.","sourceRefs":[{"relPath":"src/handlers/orders.ts","startLine":51,"endLine":57},{"relPath":"src/errors.ts","startLine":40,"endLine":48}]},{"id":"F3","title":"elapsed() returns seconds but is documented as milliseconds","severity":"medium","category":"correctness","description":"elapsed() divides by 1000, so /health reports uptimeMs in seconds. Its doc comment and docs/api.md both say milliseconds.","sourceRefs":[{"relPath":"src/lib/format.ts","startLine":3,"endLine":10},{"relPath":"src/handlers/health.ts","startLine":8,"endLine":15}]}]}